NCMAT v7
#
# A difficult test kernel for kernel sampling tests.
#
# Its H kernel has a quasi-elastic peak on the beta=0 row, where S falls roughly
# as 1/alpha from 2e7 at the smallest alpha (1.5e-5), while the neighbouring
# beta rows (+-5.8e-6) have S~150 there. Samplers bounding S by its maximum over
# a rectangle in (alpha,beta), like the strips of SABBetaStripSampler next to
# beta=0, therefore reject most proposals.
#
# It is essentially a trimmed low-precision version of the H kernel in JENDL-5
# tsl_H(C2H6O)_0606.dat based on an original conversion to NCMAT by
# J. I. Marquez Damian. This version here is not suitable for usage as anything
# other than testing purposes.
#
@DENSITY
  1.0 g_per_cm3
@STATEOFMATTER
  liquid
